{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1036604-quick-question-about-dodge","id":1036604,"title":"Quick question about Dodge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-23T07:25:25-08:00","id":1036604,"title":"Quick question about Dodge","content":"In the CofD book page 88-89 it says that you double Defense when dodging. I assume this means that you also double the skill component of Defense, so a character with Defense 2 and Athletics 2 has a total of 8 dice when dodging and not just 6 (double base Defense + unmodified Athletics).<br /> <br /> ...or have I been doing it wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:33:16-08:00","id":1036608,"title":"","content":"Wait, how did you calculate that Defense score? Defense equals the lower of Wits or Dexterity + Athletics or some replacement Skill. That Attribute + Skill score constitutes the basic Defense score, which is doubled for Dodge dice.<br /> <br /> It seems you ran with Defense = Attribute. So in this case Defense would be 2 (Attribute) + 2 (Athletics) = 4. Double that, and you get 8 for Dodge.<br /> <br /> ...Well the result is the same, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:57:47-08:00","id":1036624,"title":"","content":"My example character has 2 Wits, 2 Dexterity + 2 Athletics = 4 Defense.<br /> <br /> I take it that I calculate correctly; when dodging, this character gets 8 Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:13:01-08:00","id":1036636,"title":"","content":"Yes, you're doubling the total pool, not just the attribute","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:19:17-08:00","id":1036643,"title":"","content":"You have it right.<br /> <br /> If you're in combat situations often you might want to get some sort of Defense booster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T09:18:16-08:00","id":1036672,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that Defense removes dice directly from the attacker. Good rule of thumb is that 3 dice is 1 success. Dodge doesn't reduce attackers dice pool. You roll the Dodge Pool, and then remove your successes from attackers successes. So you can assume that you should ignore about 1 enemy success per 3 Dodge Dice rolled. Deciding to Dodge is a hard call, because while it should give you better protection, it will also take away your action; so unless you can achieve your objective without taking actions, it might be unwise to Dodge. Of course, &quot;running away&quot; is a great objective that can be achieved while Dodging. <br /> If you want to optimize your Dodge chances, remember to spent Willpower on Defense; it will give you +2 Defense, which will get doubled, netting you +4 Dodge. <br /> Can you Willpower a Dodge roll itself, by the way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:43:42-08:00","id":1037007,"title":"","content":"I have actually also thought about using a WP on a Dodge roll. Since the Dodge roll does not directly subtract dice from an enemy but is a contested action like any other, a spent WP should give +3 rather than +2. That's how I've done it as a Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:50:38-08:00","id":1037013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1036604-quick-question-about-dodge?p=1037007#post1037007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have actually also thought about using a WP on a Dodge roll. Since the Dodge roll does not directly subtract dice from an enemy but is a contested action like any other, a spent WP should give +3 rather than +2. That's how I've done it as a Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Defense does directly subtract dice from an enemy's dice pool. And the dice pool for Dodging is equal to twice your Defense. What WHW is suggesting is that you spend Willpower to give yourself +2 Defense first and then Dodge, so you double that and get a total of +4 dice on your Dodge pool instead of +3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:03:29-08:00","id":1037021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1036604-quick-question-about-dodge?p=1037013#post1037013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Defense does directly subtract dice from an enemy's dice pool. And the dice pool for Dodging is equal to twice your Defense. What WHW is suggesting is that you spend Willpower to give yourself +2 Defense first and then Dodge, so you double that and get a total of +4 dice on your Dodge pool instead of +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I am tired and did not pay enough attention to their post. It seems like a nifty trick, though one I as a ST would not personally allow. Maybe I would use it myself though as a player if the ST allows it. I'm a horrible, soulless, post-modern, post-industrial, millenial hypocrite that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:08:37-08:00","id":1037023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1036604-quick-question-about-dodge?p=1037021#post1037021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I am tired and did not pay enough attention to their post. It seems like a nifty trick, though one I as a ST would not personally allow. Maybe I would use it myself though as a player if the ST allows it. I'm a horrible, soulless, post-modern, post-industrial, millenial hypocrite that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T21:18:43-08:00","id":1037039,"title":"","content":"I'm asking about this because I remember being told that there is no limit of how many Willpower points you can spend in 2nd ED per turn, being only limited by one per action, so I was wondering if you could do a Hyper Dodge by WPing for +2 Defence, Dodging to make it double, and then spending Willpower to enhance the roll by adding +3 to it, netting you a total of +7 Dodge dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-24-2017, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T21:21:37-08:00","id":1037040,"title":"","content":"If you're not Defending, you're not using a Defense action. You'd probably be better off getting the 3 from the Dodge than 2 from Defense, which likely wouldn't be doubled.<br /> <br /> Though obviously you can do whatever you want at your own table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-24-2017, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T22:42:21-08:00","id":1037054,"title":"","content":"I can't find it, so it might have been in the GMCRU instead of 2e core, but IIRC somewhere it says that bonuses to Defense (such as from equipment) aren't doubled. This would mean that spending WP as per a roll would be superior.<br /> <br /> Spending WP on Defense and then on Dodge would not work though, because neither raises them for more than one action. You can't spend more than one WP per action, even as a defender, and that would be spending two WP against one attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}